Subject: [PATCH] Handle backends without a control ring

If the backend does not advertise feature-ctrl-ring, ControllerConnect()
sets up no ring and leaves Controller->Connected clear. Requests used to
fail with STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED in that case, and the frontend ignored that
for the default (UNSPECIFIED) hash algorithm. Two changes have broken this:

- 50957a5 "Fix argument to ControllerSetHashAlgorithm" made
  __FrontendUpdateHash() treat UNSPECIFIED like NONE, and so check the
  result of setting XEN_NETIF_CTRL_HASH_ALGORITHM_NONE.

- a9e785f "Check controller enable status in PutRequest" replaced the
  Connected check in ControllerPutRequest() with Enabled, which
  ControllerEnable() sets unconditionally. A request now gets as far as
  RING_FULL(), which is always true for a ring that was never initialized,
  and fails with STATUS_INSUFFICIENT_RESOURCES.

As a result FrontendEnable() fails on such a backend, XENNET cannot restart
its miniport and the device ends up with CM_PROB_FAILED_POST_START.

Only enable the controller if it is connected, so that it never accepts a
request it has no ring for, and add ControllerIsEnabled() so that
__FrontendUpdateHash() can leave the controller alone in that case. Hashing
cannot be configured without a control ring, so there is nothing to do
unless a hash is being asked for, and that fails with STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED
(XENNET then does not advertise RSS).

Nothing else uses the control ring, and the remaining Controller*() calls
made by the frontend already cope with Connected being clear.
---
Not part of the commit message:
 * Against xenvif master c042e3b.
 * patches/xenvif-ctrl-ring-fix.patch in this repository is the same change
   against the revision our build pins (0c61248).
 * Add the Signed-off-by before sending.

  src/xenvif/controller.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
  src/xenvif/controller.h |  7 ++++++-
  src/xenvif/frontend.c   | 11 +++++++++++
  3 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/xenvif/controller.c b/src/xenvif/controller.c
index f5dc178..53910a2 100644
--- a/src/xenvif/controller.c
+++ b/src/xenvif/controller.c
@@ -684,12 +684,14 @@ fail1:
 
 VOID
 ControllerEnable(
-    _Out_ PXENVIF_CONTROLLER    Controller
+    _Inout_ PXENVIF_CONTROLLER  Controller
     )
 {
     __ControllerAcquireLock(Controller);
 
-    Controller->Enabled = TRUE;
+    // Requests can only be accepted if ControllerConnect() set up a
+    // control ring, which it does not do unless the backend offers one.
+    Controller->Enabled = Controller->Connected;
 
     __ControllerReleaseLock(Controller);
 
@@ -710,6 +712,14 @@ ControllerDisable(
     Trace("<===>\n");
 }
 
+BOOLEAN
+ControllerIsEnabled(
+    _In_ PXENVIF_CONTROLLER Controller
+    )
+{
+    return Controller->Enabled;
+}
+
 _IRQL_requires_(DISPATCH_LEVEL)
 VOID
 ControllerDisconnect(
diff --git a/src/xenvif/controller.h b/src/xenvif/controller.h
index 39eab1f..8de634e 100644
--- a/src/xenvif/controller.h
+++ b/src/xenvif/controller.h
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@ ControllerStoreWrite(
 
 extern VOID
 ControllerEnable(
-    _Out_ PXENVIF_CONTROLLER    Controller
+    _Inout_ PXENVIF_CONTROLLER  Controller
     );
 
 extern VOID
@@ -71,6 +71,11 @@ ControllerDisable(
     _Out_ PXENVIF_CONTROLLER    Controller
     );
 
+extern BOOLEAN
+ControllerIsEnabled(
+    _In_ PXENVIF_CONTROLLER Controller
+    );
+
 _IRQL_requires_(DISPATCH_LEVEL)
 extern VOID
 ControllerDisconnect(
diff --git a/src/xenvif/frontend.c b/src/xenvif/frontend.c
index b1701cf..f1ab7e8 100644
--- a/src/xenvif/frontend.c
+++ b/src/xenvif/frontend.c
@@ -2090,6 +2090,17 @@ __FrontendUpdateHash(
         return STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED;
     }
 
+    // Hashing is configured using the control ring. If the controller is
+    // not accepting requests, which it never does if the backend has no
+    // control ring, then no hash can be configured. This is not a problem
+    // unless one is being asked for: there is nothing to turn off.
+    if (!ControllerIsEnabled(Controller)) {
+        if (NetifAlgorithm == XEN_NETIF_CTRL_HASH_ALGORITHM_NONE)
+            goto done;
+
+        return STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED;
+    }
+
     status = ControllerSetHashAlgorithm(Controller,
                                         NetifAlgorithm);
     if (!NT_SUCCESS(status))
